* Small-signal common-emitter amplifier (low frequency)
* The BJT is replaced by its hybrid-pi small-signal equivalent, built from
* a resistor (r_pi) and a voltage-controlled current source (VCCS, g_m * v_be).
* This is the "controlled-source + resistor network" model of the transistor.

.title Small-Signal Common-Emitter Amplifier (hybrid-pi model)

* --- Hybrid-pi small-signal BJT subcircuit (low frequency) ---
* r_pi : base-emitter input resistance
* g_m  : transconductance; the VCCS current g_m * v_be flows from collector to emitter.
*        (VCCS syntax: G <name> n+ n- nc+ nc- gm; current leaves n+ and enters n-)
.subckt ssbjt base collector emitter
Rpi base emitter 4k
Gm  emitter collector base emitter 40m
.ends

* Input signal source: 1 kHz / 10 mV sine wave (small signal)
Vin in 0 sin(0 0.01 1k)

* In the small-signal equivalent the DC supply VCC becomes AC ground,
* so the bias resistors now connect the base to ground.
R1 in 0 27k
R2 in 0 3.9k

* Hybrid-pi BJT; the emitter is AC-grounded (fully bypassed by CE at mid-band).
X1 in out 0 ssbjt

* Collector load and load resistor; their VCC end is AC-ground.
RC out 0 2.2k
RL out 0 10k

.tran 1e-5 0.005
.end